{"availability":"available","full":"bpyman/onfile","name":"onfile","description":"Ask about a public company, get the number and the SEC filing behind it. An evidence-first research agent: the LLM plans, deterministic code owns every figure.","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-20T23:34:39Z","updated":"2026-10-08T20:50:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://onfile-analyst.vercel.app","topics":["ai-agent","edgar","fastapi","financial-analysis","langgraph-python","llm","mcp","nextjs","portfolio-project","python3","react","sec-edgar","typescript","xbrl"],"demo":"https://onfile-analyst.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.626Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.626Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.626Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.626Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js","Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Explore company financials, straight from SEC filings.","Ask about a company and get the number and the filing behind it. Onfile is an evidence-first research agent. A planner reads the question, rules first and a language model where the rules are unsure; deterministic code owns every number: the quarterly facts, the arithmetic, the rankings, and the values on screen. Click any figure, in a table or on a chart, to see the exact amount, CIK, accession, XBRL concept, and a link to the filing it came from.","Try the live demo · Run it locally · Design · ADRs"],"features":["Planners, on 160 held-out conversations written by another lab's model (xAI's Grok 4.7): rules planner 96%, LLM planner 94%, and the rules-first cascade 97% (comparison).","Within noise, so decided on cost: no difference between the planners is significant (p = 0.22 to 0.73). The live demo runs the cascade (ADR 0012), which sent 7% of planner calls to the LLM: $0.13 for the run against…","Everyday wording: 518 of 518 phrasings of metrics, windows, changes and follow-ups, alone and in combination, read as the defaults say (phrase coverage).","Figures checked against their filings: 25 of 25 found in the text of the 10-Q they cite (filing check).","What did not work, and what changed: retired approaches, wrong numbers, and a held-out set I had read."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bpyman/onfile/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"6ff7a0829182f0da2848d3b6055b5055df73080b61dd2593ff7a2c54b67659c3","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.798Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.798Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Explore company financials, straight from SEC filings.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bpyman/onfile/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"6ff7a0829182f0da2848d3b6055b5055df73080b61dd2593ff7a2c54b67659c3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bpyman/onfile/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.799Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T20:50:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bpyman/onfile/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:13.800Z","hash":"6ff7a0829182f0da2848d3b6055b5055df73080b61dd2593ff7a2c54b67659c3","originalBytes":40496,"storedBytes":40496,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["quarter","planner","revenue","year","docs","company","over","adr","what","quarters","every","income","run","each","how","latest","net","window","apple","change","one","evaluation","live","question","filing","metric","python","rules","companies","figure","last","sec","read","text","figures","growth","microsoft","only","recorded","api","fiscal","about","period","same","shows","changed","eps","instead","llm","margin","own","ranking","turn","which","after","against","asks","filings","months","any","financial","named","names","web","when","analyst","before","derived","first","name","note","now","out","portfolio","quarterly","reads","runtime","their","top","two","where","year